== known mismatches and why (proxy vs real search) ==
1. Variant A: proxy rescues 3, real run rescues 4. Extra case is
   pcb/translation-50: proxy closest complete evaluation had angle
   error 1.05 deg and worst fully-visible block 0.574 (9/10); the
   variant A accepted pose (calibration-a/matrix/poses.csv) is
   0.08 px / 0.04 deg from ground truth. The proxy sampled ONE pose
   ~1 deg off; the search found a nearer pose where that block
   clears 0.80. Single-pose proxy vs multi-pose search.
2. Variant B: proxy rescues 1, real run rescues 5. Extra cases:
   pcb/noise-15, metal/noise-15, metal/noise-30,
   metal/occlusion-0.1 (proxy worst blocks 0.496-0.680, support
   13-14/15 at 0.70). Their accepted poses
   (calibration-b/matrix/poses.csv) are 0.13-0.64 px / 0.04-0.79 deg
   from ground truth — the same neighbourhood as the proxy pose —
   yet the worst block clears 0.70 there. Worst-block correlation
   swings by 0.1-0.2+ under sub-pixel / sub-degree changes; the
   proxy samples one pose, the search tries hundreds and accepts
   any passing pose. The proxy therefore systematically
   underestimates rescues. Largest swing is metal/noise-30
   (0.496 -> >=0.70); which pose detail flips it is not recorded
   in the available data — that would need the accepted pose's
   per-block values.
3. Pass-sample metal/scale-0.7: proxy says REJECT under every rule
   (14/15, worst block 0.133), but stage-b, variant A and variant B
   real runs all passed it (absent from every kill list). step1
   notes the top-5 nearby evaluations include a 15/15 pose: a
   known proxy artefact, not a real regression.
4. Textured impostors at 0.70: NOT computable from cases.json
   (only dense@0.80 counts were measured). Their 0.70 blocking
   rests on the variant B 11-case real run (11/11), not on this
   program. This program reports UNKNOWN for them under variant B.
5. metal/occlusion-0.4: step1 notes its rejection is driven mainly
   by the contradiction early-return, not by the support count.
   This program models only the support-count gate, not the
   contradiction gate.

What this program does NOT verify: that the gate blocks real
impostors in a live search; that any threshold is safe for unseen
targets; speed; the full 220-case matrix; anything about the
contradiction gate, blurred rescue paths, or the dense/localized
correlation computation itself. See README.md.
